{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0aa5ee71275493ddc270b05e814695539f4c62ab8988f950459e13c9cc4c098d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"morganlinton/albatross@6f20178d81c6 snapshot efa5ca6ad18bbc10","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_88dd71f1d2cd5ebcaf256491100bc638e2692ad16e03919c13ab7c3a48b42762","slc_bce8326901b025141c687de0cb2866e37fd1f66c5524c789a0a702dcd1efa8fc"],"source_ids":["src_5664aa6a6ad353fcbf3ec91e36d43a8b"],"text":"Approval policies are always (default, prompts with diff preview), dangerous-only (prompts on non-obviously-safe mutations and strips hydrated API-key env vars from shell children), and never; per-prompt options include always-for-this-tool and session-allow for the exact call.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_104a5121b42ac65e6501769453435fc6832556e16812cebc5ec71405cbc7905f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"morganlinton/albatross@6f20178d81c6 snapshot efa5ca6ad18bbc10","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0f69694b40e40d7903e59b43c0aa52a753e8a0907b18172f4a293af07e40e593","slc_20557155591a420e2e64728517637018e16a73dbc8f25230a725b064fd628b57","slc_df17e844166534b89534c9a62ab1c2decaa3c09def62ab09e92dd3b848b20933"],"source_ids":["src_5664aa6a6ad353fcbf3ec91e36d43a8b"],"text":"The agent talks to one provider at a time, but providers can be switched mid-session with /provider while tools, commands, and the session log stay unchanged; Ollama is the default provider.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_169a5d896953bb4718358a2326a51ee6477c4cc6e10460db0f4dad53bc923e27","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"morganlinton/albatross@6f20178d81c6 snapshot efa5ca6ad18bbc10","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_25a1b184e4720768bed96d4175cf69063fa47d18fa7ed1bf46106610d4ee274b","slc_850980bbef26dac0e560fe2c73318e080ffc82e5f53455597e225988f306b504","slc_b1ddb6da5daa5f9940b34606f820519244a4ce5f6c18d2a4ce7bc1dfd5a36ce3","slc_ee50863c65e838bae52d4a3d6c3160b15d4397e15c2fe8aceb8ed0b07d3502e5"],"source_ids":["src_5664aa6a6ad353fcbf3ec91e36d43a8b"],"text":"Albatross is a terminal TUI coding agent launched via the `albatross` binary, with slash commands including /provider, /model, /plan, /ship, /undo, /auto, and `--continue` to resume the most recent session in the cwd.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_173a216713cb24d0d66f9771f92bab2b63d569a916bdc6d1445a0bd9f795e8aa","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"morganlinton/albatross@6f20178d81c6 snapshot efa5ca6ad18bbc10","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_583a51a15d19ee4fb1ad5af42809b2fc843e336b6e99934757a3b8a8051baf84","slc_a1a0a6995242101efcc0d1162b3de66387dbcd6ff2de9b9500f138bca2cbf754"],"source_ids":["src_5664aa6a6ad353fcbf3ec91e36d43a8b"],"text":"/iterate runs a generate-evaluate loop where a separate read-only critic agent scores work 0-10 against a weighted rubric; the harness itself computes the weighted total and pass/fail, and an optional evaluator model can differ from the generator.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1888bef8deb5d8db0e08c31706c228c2b77003987352aac9eeac7a629b5af2e8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"morganlinton/albatross@6f20178d81c6 snapshot efa5ca6ad18bbc10","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a5d38bef8accdb5030346e479b58c04251aa99324f27b93fa8a08fbb703d32eb"],"source_ids":["src_5664aa6a6ad353fcbf3ec91e36d43a8b"],"text":"Albatross supports the open Agent Skills directory/frontmatter standard, discovering skills from project and user roots plus installed packages; only names and descriptions enter the initial prompt, with full instructions loaded on demand.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_372a50951c15889a12c71a995249715fccdf0c21afba89ad3600cfad0a1c7747","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"morganlinton/albatross@6f20178d81c6 snapshot efa5ca6ad18bbc10","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_29a0be34efc78deb2ec09323e41170e49fd8d0910478e9165c23d07747dece5b","slc_30e822b01cf9943e33b6d5f90f90f35add591ee7413fecc0f906659e08a84b0d"],"source_ids":["src_5664aa6a6ad353fcbf3ec91e36d43a8b"],"text":"/plan route builds a low/medium/high task graph in .albatross/plan.json using a configurable planner model, and /plan execute runs ready tasks sequentially, switching backend/model per task, with --yolo for unattended auto-approval.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3783a970a91bd025085e5a00090ede0952c975b4aba919c3a5026258cc897d46","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"morganlinton/albatross@6f20178d81c6 snapshot efa5ca6ad18bbc10","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_131968743ba52990536722eabb2602d4151629a11b94f861046544ae21238ce8","slc_35b36949a7732257a8818f50785da549a3ff49dc95dd16b56b60baf00e9daaca","slc_4ea83828660467083058eb673494df0ed56f5a39de6abc1f7b27cde4bf3a9134","slc_ef1e62cb8c0d7f1918d410422925b320661cff02a22148cbfe7ef6f81d8c5064"],"source_ids":["src_5664aa6a6ad353fcbf3ec91e36d43a8b"],"text":"MCP servers and extensions are executable programs that are not auto-spawned when new or changed; users must review and trust them, trust is stored per workspace and config hash, and their tool calls remain approval-gated by default.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a3dca4499469dcfeab060e0021b7c4be17ade50d3ad8c4a7b25727a3cfee3579","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"morganlinton/albatross@6f20178d81c6 snapshot efa5ca6ad18bbc10","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_391f8aded6e7d73eab833fb2b52406d65e928e340995637b0394527531ccb1aa","slc_4051531e8d2881d9c7e8af4a7841a5e07b822c04e24d6350683e7f18091c0d80","slc_60e8ae60ae995bf73f7d9cfb784e7472b36d18cdac268170e9f9b683dd638ec9"],"source_ids":["src_5664aa6a6ad353fcbf3ec91e36d43a8b"],"text":"/auto repeats the iterate loop unattended with budget, deadline, round-ceiling, and stall-detection bounds, auto-fires /reset on context fill, and writes a report with verdict, per-round scores, criteria checklist, cost, and reset count.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ceb2ef3200344c7a98ea28eabf8f320d"}
